2: So did Dr. Ford. It's a terrible argument.

3: #MeToo is all about power difference, and this is your argument?

@tylerelives @cheesenutpea @KyleLovesBernie You can't "factually prove" most rapes, due to the nature of the crime.

When it comes to old cases, the evidence consists of timing (the two being in the same place, job loss, etc) and people the victim told back then. Tara Reade has that on her side.

#MeToo #BelieveWomen

@Changinglenses @politico I'm not trying to change your vote, I'm supporting #MeToo and Tara.

Tara literally has a voice from the grave supporting the fact that she told her story back then, long before Biden was running for president.

Biden, on the other hand, has a history of inappropriate touching.

@brianbeutler Biden has a history of sexually harassing women and inappropriate touching ON CAMERA. He's certainly not more credible than Kavanaugh.

As for Tara, please explain what makes her less credible without using smears that are unrelated to the issue at hand.

#MeToo

@peterdaou They methodically try to destroy any amount of progress made by feminists and the #MeToo movement while they're at it.

Meanwhile their party is burning to the ground, and they can't smell the smoke through their own bullshit.

Good riddance.
